{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Enumeration","symbolKind":"enum","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}],"title":"EntityCollapse","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence14EntityCollapseO"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Why-the-hook-takes-the-whole-collection","text":"Why the hook takes the whole collection","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A per-ID resolver would only handle half the problem. Rows sharing an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are one failure mode; the other is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"singleton"}]},{"text":" — an entity an app holds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exactly one of, such as a settings record. Created independently on two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fresh installs, two singletons have ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"different"}]},{"text":" UUIDs, so nothing groups","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them and no ID-keyed resolver can ever see the conflict. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"([E]) -> [E]"},{"type":"text","text":" hook covers both, plus general garbage collection, with one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"The-determinism-requirement","text":"The determinism requirement","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A resolver must be a pure function of "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"replicated content","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — never"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"persistentModelID"},{"text":", never a local timestamp, never array position. Every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"device must compute the same survivor set from the same rows. A resolver","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that doesn’t reintroduces the mutual-tombstone loss the write path is"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"designed to avoid: two devices pick different survivors, each tombstones the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"other’s, and after sync "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"both","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" rows are gone."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It must also be idempotent — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collapse(collapse(rows))"},{"text":" must keep the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"IDs as ","type":"text"},{"code":"collapse(rows)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". This is checked with an ","type":"text"},{"code":"assert","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in debug builds.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Collapse removes IDs, not rows","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Collapse-removes-IDs-not-rows"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A resolver’s output is read as "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the set of IDs that should exist and what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each should contain"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":". An ID the resolver drops is deleted, including every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row carrying it. Several rows that share a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"surviving"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ID are all updated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the survivor’s value, and none of them is deleted."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That asymmetry is deliberate, and it is the whole reason the singleton case"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is the one this hook really solves. Deleting an ID is safe because "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"replicated: every device independently computes the same set of doomed IDs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and issues the same deletions. Deleting one of several rows that share an ID"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" safe — nothing replicated distinguishes them, so two devices can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pick different physical rows to keep, each tombstones the other’s, and both"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are lost."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Rows sharing an ID need no deletion anyway: writes already converge across"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every matching row and reads already collapse to one value per ID (see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), so duplicates cost storage and nothing else."}]}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Type Methods","anchor":"Type-Methods"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse"},"references":{"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityDB":{"role":"symbol","title":"EntityDB","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityDB","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitydb","abstract":[{"text":"A generic ","type":"text"},{"code":"@ModelActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that reads and writes any ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityDB","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence","title":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityCollapse":{"role":"symbol","title":"EntityCollapse","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/PersistableModel":{"role":"symbol","title":"PersistableModel","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistableModel","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/persistablemodel","abstract":[{"text":"The generated SwiftData ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" shadow for a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableEntity","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistableModel","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityCollapse/byID(preferring:)":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"byID","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"preferring","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ([","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]) -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse\/byid(preferring:)","title":"byID(preferring:)","abstract":[{"text":"Collapses rows sharing an ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" down to one, keeping the winner of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"choose","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Rows with unique IDs pass through untouched.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)"}}}